From 00cdad12ae3ea24e3fef3f87ef0ff58dc6512ac8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nick Alonso <nick@drkm.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 02:21:01 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08/10] Inkling: dense shared experts instead of folding them
 into the routed gather

Back-to-back with mlx-vlm 0.7.11 on the same checkpoint and machine state
(bench/K2-same-hold-table.md) the fold cost 19-29% of prefill throughput at
2K-8K tokens: the two always-on experts went through the sorted gather_qmm
path instead of plain quantized GEMMs. They are now one dense SwiGLU whose
weights are concatenated at load (exact for quantized tensors), as mlx-vlm
does; the route kernel emits the routed indices and all eight weights.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
